{% extends 'AdminBundle::layout.html.twig' %}
{% import 'AdminBundle:Common:design-macros.html.twig' as design %}
{% block pagetitle %}
	<h1>Departments</h1>
	<nav>
		<button class="clean-white">Create New Department</button>
	</nav>
{% endblock %}
{% block prepage %}
    <p>The department field is the primary grouping field for tickets and chats. For many helpdesks, this will be the only field configured. A typical set of departments would include "Sales", "Support" and "Billing".</p>
    <p>The department field controls the editor for tickets and chats. For each department you can configure different forms with different categories, priorities, workflows as well as custom fields.</p>
	<p>The department field is used to configure permissions for both users and agents. Departments are global across tickets and chats; you can disable departments for a particular application if you wish. Those with the need for further granularity can create sub-departments.</p>
	<p>Please note that DeskPRO requires at least one department enabled for tickets and chats. If you only have a single department enabled, the field will not be shown to users.</p>
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="dp-page-box">

<div class="page-content" data-element-handler="DeskPRO.Admin.Departments.AjaxSave">
	{{ design.structure_table() }}
		{% for department in all_departments %}
			{% include 'AdminBundle:Departments:list-row.html.twig' %}
		{% endfor %}
	{{ design.structure_table_end() }}
</div>

</div>
{% endblock %}
